<LegalLayout title="Privacy Policy" effectiveDate="12 July 2026">
  <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
  <p>
    The Forest Network (“we,” “us,” “our”) is a private, invite-only messaging community built on
    the Matrix protocol. We run our own Synapse homeserver and a branded Element app for iOS and
    Android. The service is operated by Evan Roth and Daniel McLean. For any privacy question, or
    to access, correct or delete your information, contact Evan Roth at <a href="mailto:legal@theforestnetwork.earth">legal@theforestnetwork.earth</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Our approach and legal position</h2>
  <p>
    We are a small, non-commercial community based in Australia. Because our annual turnover is
    under A$3 million, and we are not a health service provider and do not trade in personal
    information, we fall within the small-business exemption to the Privacy Act 1988 (Cth) and are
    generally not bound by the Australian Privacy Principles. We publish this policy voluntarily —
    for transparency with our members and to meet Apple App Store and Google Play requirements. We
    honour the core rights of access, correction and deletion as a courtesy. We are not currently
    subject to the EU GDPR or the California CCPA.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Where your data is stored</h2>
  <p>
    All service data is stored on our own server located in Australia. Federation is disabled,
    which means your data is not replicated to, or shared with, any other Matrix server. The only
    routine flow of data outside our server is push notifications (see section 6).
  </p>

  <h2>4. What we collect and what we can see</h2>
  <p>To run the service, our server stores, and our administrators can technically access:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Account data — your username / Matrix ID, display name, avatar, password hash, account
      creation date, and any email address you provide for recovery.
    </li>
    <li>Device and session data — device IDs and names, access (session) tokens, and push notification keys.</li>
    <li>Network data — IP addresses and client/browser information, recorded in server logs and the database.</li>
    <li>
      Room and message information — the rooms you are in, room memberships, names and topics,
      message timestamps, reactions, read receipts, and the content of any messages and files you
      submit.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    <strong>Message visibility.</strong> All message content and file attachments are stored on
    our server in a form our administrators can technically read. We do not use end-to-end
    encryption. This is a deliberate design choice that enables new members to view the full
    history of a channel when they join. We limit administrator access to what is necessary to
    operate the service, investigate reports, and enforce our Terms of Service.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Channel history.</strong> Channel history is intentionally preserved and accessible.
    When you join a room, or sign in on a new device, you can read the full history of that
    channel. This is a core feature of the service, designed so that new members can participate
    in ongoing conversations with full context.
  </p>
  <p>
    We do not use third-party analytics, we do not profile you, we do not show advertising, and we
    do not sell or rent your data to anyone.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Why we collect it</h2>
  <p>
    We collect this information solely to operate the service: to sign you in, deliver and store
    your messages, send notifications, keep the service secure, prevent abuse, and fix problems.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Push notifications</h2>
  <p>
    If you turn on push notifications, your device obtains a push token from Apple's Push
    Notification service (APNs) or Google's Firebase Cloud Messaging (FCM). Our server sends
    notification triggers through a push gateway to APNs or FCM so your device can alert you. We
    configure push to carry minimal information — typically the event and room identifiers rather
    than message content. Apple and Google process this data under their own privacy policies.
    This is the only routine situation in which limited data leaves our Australian server, and it
    is sent to providers located outside Australia.
  </p>

  <h2>7. How long we keep it</h2>
  <p>
    We keep your account information for as long as your account exists. Messages you send remain
    part of the room's history and are not automatically deleted when you delete your account,
    consistent with the channel-history design described in section 4 — you can delete individual
    messages yourself, or ask us to remove specific content. Technical logs, including IP and
    last-seen records, are kept only as long as needed to operate and secure the service and are
    then deleted on a rolling basis.
  </p>
  <p>
    Deleting your account removes your devices, access tokens, push records and password hash, and
    removes you from rooms and the user directory. It does not delete messages you have already
    sent — these remain visible in room history to other members, as described above. Because
    federation is disabled, there are no copies on other servers — deletion of your account data on
    our server is complete.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Security</h2>
  <p>
    We take reasonable technical and organisational steps to protect your information, including
    encrypted transport (TLS), access controls on the server, and limiting administrator access to
    what is needed to run the service. No system is perfectly secure. If a breach occurs that is
    likely to cause you serious harm, we will notify affected members and provide guidance, even
    though we are not legally required to do so.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Your choices and rights</h2>
  <p>You can:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Access and update much of your information directly in the app — display name, avatar, devices and sessions;</li>
    <li>Request a copy of your data, or ask us to correct it;</li>
    <li>Delete your account from within the app at any time, which removes your data as described in section 7.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    To make any request or complaint, contact Evan Roth at <a href="mailto:legal@theforestnetwork.earth">legal@theforestnetwork.earth</a>. If you are not
    satisfied with our response, you may contact the Office of the Australian Information
    Commissioner at <a href="https://oaic.gov.au" target="_blank" rel="noopener">oaic.gov.au</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Children</h2>
  <p>
    The service is invite-only and intended for adults. We do not knowingly collect information
    from children under 18.
  </p>

  <h2>11. Changes</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this policy. The current version is always available at this address, with the
    “last updated” date shown above.
  </p>

  <h2>12. Contact</h2>
  <p>Evan Roth — <a href="mailto:legal@theforestnetwork.earth">legal@theforestnetwork.earth</a></p>
</LegalLayout>
